   DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION TO SELL TEXT TERMINALS BUSINESS
     TO ALL-QUOTES, INC. SUBSIDIARY SUNRIVER DATA SYSTEMS, INC.


MAYNARD, Mass. -- August 30, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
(NYSE::DEC) and SunRiver Data Systems, Inc., a wholly owned 
subsidiary of All-Quotes, Inc. (NASDAQ::ALQT), of Austin, Texas 
today announced that they have completed a memorandum of 
understanding (MOU) to sell Digital's text terminals product 
business to SunRiver.  The proposed sale is subject various 
contingencies including the negotiation of definitive agreements 
and securing government approval. 

     Under the terms of the MOU, Digital and SunRiver will enter 
into a long-term supply agreement under which SunRiver will provide 
Digital with text terminals for its customers.  In addition, 
Digital will continue to service its customers' present text 
terminals.  The companies intend to enter into an agreement under 
which Digital will service VT and Dorio text terminals to be 
manufactured by SunRiver. The transfer of the business is expected 
to be completed by the fall of 1995.  Digital will retain its 
Multia multi-client desktop line of products that enable users to 
work across multiple computing environments. 

     Charles F. Christ, vice president and general manager of 
Digital's Components Division, commented, "While the text terminals 
business has been a key part of Digital's historical product line, 
this sale supports our growth strategy of focusing our investments 
in our core competencies and divesting in areas where we cannot 
differentiate ourselves."

     "This transaction will allow SunRiver to better service our 
customers through the addition of the respected VT and Dorio 
product lines, while complementing our existing	business," said 
Gerald Youngblood, chairman and president of SunRiver.  "We look 
forward to a long-term relationship with Digital and its loyal 
customers and partners." 

     The Chase Manhattan Bank, N.A. is acting as advisor to 
SunRiver on the transaction.  Further details of the MOU are 
confidential by mutual consent of the companies.  

     SunRiver Data Systems is a leading producer of text and 
MultiConsole terminals, X-stations, and systems software and 
services.  Headquartered in Austin, Texas, SunRiver Data Systems 
maintains additional manufacturing and R&D facilities in Hauppauge, 
New York and Orlando, Florida.  Another wholly owned subsidiary of 
All-Quotes, Inc. is TradeWave Corporation, also based in Austin, 
Texas, which provides software, services and consulting to enable 
electronic commerce on the Internet.  TradeWave helps businesses 
build and operate Virtual Private Internets (VPI)s, and it also 
publishes Galaxy, a highly acclaimed Internet directory service for 
locating information on the Internet.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused	solutions from business partners, help organizations 
compete and win in today's global marketplace.
