        DIGITAL STRENGTHENS THIRD-PARTY APPLICATION PORTFOLIO
                WITH NEW SOFTWARE DEVELOPERS PROGRAM


MAYNARD, Mass., September 18, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation
today announced a program designed to further strengthen its
rapidly growing portfolio of third-party software applications. 

     The new Association of Software & Application Partners offers a
broad range of incentives to developers to make it easier and more
attractive for them to develop software applications on and for
Digital platforms.  

     "This program provides superior incentives -- from aggressive 
financial plans, to unrestricted access to software development 
experts and facilities, to marketing and training support," said 
Mike Gallup, Digital vice president of Worldwide Systems Marketing.  
"For software vendors who want to do business on the industry's 
fastest and most cost-effective workstations and servers, membership 
in this program is a key path."

     Today, more than 7,000 software applications are available on 
Digital's family of 64-bit AlphaServer and AlphaStation systems.  
This growing list of applications include those critical to the 
success of professionals working in technical and commercial 
application areas -- from graphics-intensive design markets to those 
required in workgroup and enterprise-level computing environments.    

     "Our Alpha systems quickly are becoming the preferred platform 
among power users who crave raw performance and want the industry's 
leading levels of price/performance.  When combined with Digital's 
Intel based platform, we offer leading price/performance advantages 
at the key price points," Gallup said.  "The Association clearly 
benefits those developers who want to do business on our systems.  
And of course, Digital benefits as well.  But it's the customers 
who'll benefit the most.  Customers will acquire greater software 
application choices, whether they're running 64-bit Digital UNIX, 
OpenVMS or the Windows NT operating system."

     The Association is a foundation of services for Digital 
partners who provide software value.  Regardless of any existing 
relationship with Digital, members of the new Association will 
receive a significantly increased level of responsiveness.

The program provides the following critical services to its 
members:

     o 	Enhanced access to software application development, testing 
        and demonstration equipment as well as aggressive financial 
        terms -- up to 50 percent off some systems, for example.  
        Members also may make use of a Digital Development Center 
        which contain the latest AlphaServers and AlphaStations and 
        other Digital platforms.
 
     o 	Expert technical and business support assistance with a
     	guaranteed 24-hour response time.  Members requiring support 
        can contact Digital product experts through unlimited use of 
        a toll-free telephone number, electronic mail and through 
        Digital's Partner Network -- a private electronic 
        bulletin-board.

     o 	Marketing services and tools designed to enhance the 
        partner's "go to market" success.  These include sales kits, 
        direct marketing services, seminars, a listing in the Alpha 
        Applications Catalog and use of Digital's Business Partner 
        relationship logo.

     o 	Comprehensive and frequent communications designed to foster
     	close collaboration between Digital and Association members. 
     	Association members will receive hardcopy and electronic
     	publications that keep them up-to-date on the latest 
        product, corporate and partnership news.  Members also may 
        have their home page on the World Wide Web hot linked to the 
        Digital home page for even greater information access.

     o  A dedicated representative to provide a convenient "one stop
     	shopping" approach for members requiring technical support 
        or wishing to conduct other business with Digital.
     
     	Software developers seeking additional information on the  
        program should call 1-800-332-4786.

     Digital provides the industry's broadest range of 64-bit
workstations and servers -- all based on the Alpha architecture. The 
company's recently introduced AlphaStation 600 series delivers 
advanced graphics, multimedia, and collaborative capabilities -- and 
50 to 150 percent better real-world applications performance that 
competitive workstations.  Digital's AlphaServer 8400, part of a 
scalable family of servers, delivers more than three times the 
performance of the competition's fastest offering and supports the 
most demanding large commercial, technical and multi-user 
applications.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's marketplace.
