                   DIGITAL SHOWS NEW CHIP, NETWORK
            PERFORMANCE, FLEXIBILITY AT NETWORLD+INTEROP


 ...21140A PCI Fast Ethernet Demos, PC Giveaway Highlight Exhibit...


ATLANTA, Georgia, September 27, 1995 -- The industry's most popular 
and most  powerful Ethernet connectivity devices for PCI systems 
highlight the  exhibit by Digital Semiconductor, a Digital Equipment 
Corporation  business, at Networld+Interop Fall '95, open today 
through Friday at the Georgia World Congress Center.

     Located at Booth 1760, the exhibit features Digital's market-
leading PCI Fast Ethernet chips, the 21140 and new 21140A, and 
focuses on demonstrations of their superior network performance, 
compatibility, and flexibility.

     "Digital was a pioneer in the development of PCI Ethernet 
solutions and holds the largest share of the market for PCI Ethernet 
and PCI Fast Ethernet devices," said William N. Johnson, Digital 
Semiconductor's vice president, Sales and Marketing.  "Our booth 
theme, 'If You're Not Getting There First, Ask Yourself Why,' points 
to our first-to-the-market position with PCI Ethernet chips as well 
as the performance and connectivity leadership of our network chip 
products for both 10Mbps (megabit-per-second) and 100Mbps 
applications."

Stepping Up to Fast Ethernet

     A "bricks and bridges" demonstration uses Digital's 21140 and 
21140A chips to show the advantage of upgrading to Fast Ethernet 
networks.  The demonstration contrasts 100Mbps with 10Mbps network 
throughput as "data bricks" of different colors are assembled 
graphically to form bridge piers and decks.

Multiplatform Connectivity

     The booth also includes a demonstration of network inter-
operability, connecting various platforms, including Digital's 
Alpha, Apple Macintosh, and Intel X86 systems.  A switch from 
Alantec, Inc., and 21140 chips from Digital provide intersystem 
links.

     Other Digital Semiconductor booth features include an active 
demonstration of Fast Ethernet support for T4 and TX cabling, and 
displays of board products and packaged assemblies from 
manufacturers that use Digital Semiconductor's networking products.

PC Giveaway

     Show attendees can also qualify for a drawing to win a free 
Digital Celebris Pentium 90 personal computer, packaged with an 
Ethernet adapter card based on the 21140 chip.  Entry flyers and 
instructions are available at the Digital Semiconductor booth.  
Individuals who obtain at least six validation stickers from 
companies using Digital's networking chips will receive a free 
T-shirt and qualify for the drawing. Participating companies and 
booth numbers where validation stickers for the drawing can be 
obtained include:

