             DIGITAL AND MONDADORI IN JOINT AGREEMENT
       TO LAUNCH MULTIMEDIA PROGRAMS FOR PROFESSIONAL PC MARKET
       

MILAN, Italy -- September 29, 1995 --- Within the framework of a 
broader agreement covering the development of multimedia 
solutions for the business market, Digital Equipment Corporation 
International (Europe) and Arnoldo Mondadori Editore have 
demonstrated a prototype of their first multimedia software 
application called ANTISTRESS at the SMAU Computer Fair in Milan, 
Italy.  

The CD ROM program, expected to be introduced in October, has 
been developed to analyse and reduce individual stress and can be
used in a PC-based professional working environment.
         
The ANTISTRESS CD ROM is the fruition of joint research carried 
out by the two companies and aims to be an educational, useful 
and entertaining response to user needs, particularly in business 
and professional environments.
         
The multimedia application provides an instructive and effective
exploration of stress-related issues, through a series of 
targeted graphics, digital sound and film clips, and illustrates 
the more enjoyable ways of avoiding them. Various techniques are 
addressed gradually, as the program allows step-by-step access to 
topics of personal interest for users, while suggesting remedies 
for a variety of situations. ANTISTRESS also has a glossary and a
learning guide.
         
"This CD-based application initially will be bundled with Digital 
Celebris GL products, and subsequently with all Digital PCs 
featuring a CD-ROM configuration," says Carlo Gilardi, Vice 
President, Marketing, for Digital's Personal Computer Business 
Unit in Europe.  "We also plan to pre-install a special version 
on the hard disk unit of all Digital PCs without CD-ROM.  The 
application will be a progressive step forward for users, 
providing them with better work tools through Digital PC 
products."
         
"This new software is innovative in many ways, quite beyond its 
product quality, in that the program was developed with the 
contribution of worldwide experts in psychology, medicine and 
software design," says Kurt Hilgenberg, responsible for the 
project at Mondadori.

Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
         
The Arnoldo Mondadori Editore Group, based in Milan, is the
leading Italian publishing house with more than 5,000 employees 
and contributing staff. Headed by Franco Tatr, Managing Director, 
the Group operates in five main areas: books, periodicals, 
graphics, direct marketing and advertising. The Group heads up 
some of the most prestigious Italian publishing houses including 
Elemond and Einaudi. 
